transcript.text:
Probably normal. Many Samsung combi microwaves keep the cooling fan running for a few minutes after cooking has ended, especially after convection, grill, or longer/high-power microwave use. It cools the magnetron/electronics and may continue even if you open the door; opening the door stops cooking, not necessarily the cooling cycle.

It should switch off by itself after the unit has cooled — often within a few minutes, sometimes longer after a hot oven/grill programme.

Worth checking / getting help if:

• it runs for a long time after only a very short, low-power use (e.g. 15–30+ minutes);
• it runs when the microwave has not been used and is cold;
• there is a burning smell, excessive heat, error code, rattling/grinding noise, or poor cooking performance;
• the vents are blocked or the appliance is tightly enclosed.

Make sure the exterior vents have clearance and aren’t covered. Don’t routinely unplug it just to stop the fan. The exact behaviour is usually described as “cooling fan” or “automatic cooling” in the manual for your specific Samsung model.
